#
# clang-tidy configuration, the clang half of L-19 portao 3 (cppcheck is the other half,
# see .github/workflows/cppcheck.yml). The set is CONSERVATIVE and is declared here so it
# is versioned. It grows only by an explicit decision of the project lead, never as a
# side effect of a cleanup.
#
# Why these checks:
#   bugprone-macro-parentheses          a macro argument used without parentheses changes meaning
#   bugprone-use-after-move             a moved-from object is read again
#   bugprone-unused-return-value        a result that carries the error is dropped
#   clang-analyzer-core.NullDereference a path-sensitive analyzer check, a real crash path
#   performance-unnecessary-value-param a by-value parameter that forces a copy for nothing
#   readability-braces-around-statements a branch without braces is where edits go wrong
#   readability-container-size-empty   size() == 0 is the wrong idiom for an empty test
#
# WarningsAsErrors is deliberately NOT set here. Setting it in this file would turn the
# warnings into errors in the developer's editor too. The CI job passes
# --warnings-as-errors on the command line only, so the promotion affects the gate and
# nothing else.
Checks: '-*,bugprone-macro-parentheses,bugprone-use-after-move,bugprone-unused-return-value,clang-analyzer-core.NullDereference,performance-unnecessary-value-param,readability-braces-around-statements,readability-container-size-empty'
